From 307744c4fb8427771040212988d35a50a04e2c8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Egor 835 <egor.su.8@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:34:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64: dts: msm8953-audio: Drop slimbus DAIs from the
 internal codec card

The internal codec sound card lists 30 asoc-cpu phandles but only 22
asoc-cpu-names. The machine driver matches dai links to cpu nodes by
name index, so every DAI after the MI2S ports was bound 8 entries off:
INT_BT_SCO_RX got the slimbus 0 DAI and the BT SCO DAI ended up on
INCALL_RECORD_RX. Bluetooth calls had no audio ("can't get playback BE
for Internal BT-SCO Playback"). Match msm8937-audio.dtsi.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/vendor/qcom/msm8953-audio.dtsi | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/vendor/qcom/msm8953-audio.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/vendor/qcom/msm8953-audio.dtsi
index 23ab0598a..a21ac0cbf 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/vendor/qcom/msm8953-audio.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/vendor/qcom/msm8953-audio.dtsi
@@ -98,8 +98,6 @@
 			<&dai_mi2s0>, <&dai_mi2s1>,
 			<&dai_mi2s2>, <&dai_mi2s3>,
 			<&dai_mi2s4>, <&dai_mi2s5>,
-			<&sb_0_rx>, <&sb_0_tx>, <&sb_1_rx>, <&sb_1_tx>,
-			<&sb_3_rx>, <&sb_3_tx>, <&sb_4_rx>, <&sb_4_tx>,
 			<&bt_sco_rx>, <&bt_sco_tx>,
 			<&int_fm_rx>, <&int_fm_tx>,
 			<&afe_pcm_rx>, <&afe_pcm_tx>,
-- 
